+// The D-110 firmware writes the switch-scan latch with more than a scan strobe in it:
+// bits 1-3 carry the reverb type shown on the panel, and bit 0 is the only bit that
+// moves while the panel is being scanned.
+//
+// Type 1 through 8 and OFF give 0, 2, 2, 4, 4, 6, 6, 8 in bits 1-3, which is the type
+// index with its low bit dropped; that low bit is written separately, to bit 2 of the
+// external latch at 0x0800. The reverb chip takes five data bits and two strobes built
+// from the gate array's EXIO outputs, so a four-bit type arriving over two ports is
+// what its wiring implies.
+void roland_d10_state::sw_scan_w(uint8_t data)
+{
+	m_sw_scan = data;
+}
